recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two things this round found want your word rather than another lap. %493 is OPEN and not mine: a guard seated at `tier lap` this hour refuses on any tree with no `seed/` projection, and no lap makes one, so every ship without a projection reds each lap and pays an 826-second cold pass; the roster's own `capability` field answers it, and the owning lane sits beside custody gate %1. And both living pins are full -- the ledger had NINE bytes when I went to book a red I had caused, so the row could only be written by folding it straight back out, and the card took five trims to hold one paragraph. Otherwise kg: the lane's next door is the source's own port discovery, since halving a shared resource is not removing it and `tools/fixtures/a/amphora_vessel_port_lock.sh` still keeps two lawful runs from meeting.
